    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0816" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6511/1028</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aide-Mémoire</hi>
                </p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of State and
                    has the honour to acknowledge the receipt of Mr. Hull’s note of April
                        10th<anchor n="12" xml:id="d799-f1"/> regarding the return to Europe of
                    Admiral Alberto Lais, former Naval Attaché at the Italian Embassy in Washington,
                    and his two Italian naval orderlies, Gaetano Canepa and Giovanni Burlo.</p>
                <pb facs="0817" n="805" xml:id="pg805"/>
                <p>This matter has been referred to His Majesty’s Government who have now authorized
                    Lord Halifax to give the assurance that the British authorities will not attempt
                    to prevent the return of Admiral Lais or his orderlies to Europe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-17">April 17,
                            1941</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
